# Copy this file to /etc/topotrace/topotrace.env and edit it -- systemd loads
# it via EnvironmentFile= in topotrace.service. Every setting below is
# optional; an unset/commented-out line keeps topotrace's own built-in
# default (see cmd/topotrace/main.go and topotrace-server.sh).
#
# This file can contain a real secret (TOPOTRACE_AUTH_TOKEN, and
# TOPOTRACE_POSTGRES_DSN if your DSN embeds a password) -- install.sh sets
# its permissions to 640, owned by root:topotrace, so only root and the
# topotrace service account can read it. Keep it that way; don't loosen it.

# --- Network ---
# TOPOTRACE_INGEST_ADDR=:9090
# TOPOTRACE_API_ADDR=:8080

# --- Storage ---
# Leave TOPOTRACE_POSTGRES_DSN unset to use the default JSON-snapshot store
# under TOPOTRACE_DATA_DIR (fine for evaluating TopoTrace or a small fleet).
# Set it to switch to Postgres -- see internal/store/pgstore/migrations
# for the schema it creates on first connect, applied automatically.
# TOPOTRACE_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/topotrace/data
# TOPOTRACE_POSTGRES_DSN=postgres://topotrace:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/topotrace?sslmode=disable

# --- Auth ---
# Shared secret agents present (TOPOTRACE1/TOPOTRACE1-RESULT) and API writes
# require. Always resolves to the "admin" role -- use it to bootstrap
# named API keys with narrower roles via POST /api/keys. Leaving this
# unset disables auth entirely (fine for a private LAN eval, not for
# anything reachable beyond that).
# TOPOTRACE_AUTH_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# --- Webhooks ---
# Comma-separated URLs to POST a small JSON event to on policy
# violations and remediation. Leave unset to disable.
# TOPOTRACE_WEBHOOK_URLS=https://hooks.example.com/topotrace

# --- Background evaluator ---
# How often every host is re-checked against every persisted policy
# rule (posture scoring, auto-remediation). No effect until at least one
# rule exists (POST /api/policies).
# TOPOTRACE_EVALUATOR_INTERVAL=5m

# --- Live vulnerability feed ---
# Supplements the static CVE dataset with live OSV.dev lookups. Off by
# default -- turning it on means this server makes outbound HTTPS
# requests to api.osv.dev on TOPOTRACE_VULN_FEED_INTERVAL. Set to any
# non-empty value (e.g. "true") to enable.
# TOPOTRACE_VULN_FEED=true
# TOPOTRACE_VULN_FEED_INTERVAL=6h

# --- OAuth2/OIDC dashboard login ---
# All of these are required together, or leave every one unset to keep
# browser login off entirely (bearer tokens still work either way).
# See docs/security-model.md and the top-level README's "OAuth2/OIDC
# dashboard login" section.
# TOPOTRACE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# TOPOTRACE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TOPOTRACE_OAUTH_AUTH_URL=https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth
# TOPOTRACE_OAUTH_TOKEN_URL=https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token
# TOPOTRACE_OAUTH_USERINFO_URL=https://openidconnect.googleapis.com/v1/userinfo
# TOPOTRACE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=https://topotrace.example.internal/api/auth/callback
# TOPOTRACE_OAUTH_SCOPES=
# TOPOTRACE_OAUTH_ROLE_MAP=admin@example.com=admin,*@example.com=readonly
